## Framework-Specific Rules

### When working with this project:

1. **Always use the existing architecture patterns**
2. **Follow the established file structure**
3. **Use Prisma for all database operations**
4. **Implement proper authentication for admin routes**
5. **Validate inputs at controller level**
6. **Handle errors gracefully with appropriate HTTP status codes**
7. **Use TypeScript interfaces for all data structures**
8. **Follow the existing naming conventions**
9. **Test all changes thoroughly**
10. **Update documentation when adding new features**

### Current Models & Relationships:
- **Admin**: Authentication and authorization for admin panel
- **User**: Website user accounts with e-commerce features
- **Category**: Work categorization with image support
- **Work**: Portfolio items with main image and additional images
- **Image**: Standalone image management
- **Text**: Content management with publishing workflow

### Database Schema (Prisma Models):
```typescript
// Admin model
model Admin {
  id           String   @id @default(cuid())
  username     String   @unique
  passwordHash String
  email        String   @unique
  isActive     Boolean  @default(true)
  lastLoginAt  DateTime?
  createdAt    DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt    DateTime @updatedAt
}

// User model (Website users)
model User {
  id              String    @id @default(cuid())
  name            String
  email           String    @unique
  passwordHash    String
  isActive        Boolean   @default(true)
  emailVerified   Boolean   @default(false)
  lastLoginAt     DateTime?
  shoppingCart    String?   // JSON string of cart items
  favoriteProducts String?  // JSON string of favorite product IDs
  createdAt       DateTime  @default(now())
  updatedAt       DateTime  @updatedAt
}
```

### API Endpoints Structure:

#### **Admin Endpoints** (`/api/admin/*`):
- `POST /api/admin/login` - Admin authentication
- `POST /api/admin/create-admin` - Create admin (dev only)
- `GET /api/admin/profile` - Get admin profile
- `GET /api/admin/users/stats` - **User statistics for dashboard**
- `GET /api/admin/users` - **Get all users with pagination**
- `GET /api/admin/users/:id` - **Get specific user details**
- `PUT /api/admin/users/:id/activate` - **Activate user account**
- `PUT /api/admin/users/:id/deactivate` - **Deactivate user account**

#### **User Endpoints** (`/api/users/*`):
- `POST /api/users/register` - **User registration**
- `POST /api/users/login` - **User login**
- `GET /api/users/profile` - **Get user profile (protected)**
- `PUT /api/users/profile` - **Update user profile (protected)**
- `DELETE /api/users/account` - **Deactivate user account (protected)**

#### **Shopping Cart Endpoints** (`/api/users/cart/*`):
- `PUT /api/users/cart` - **Update entire shopping cart**
- `POST /api/users/cart/add` - **Add item to cart**
- `DELETE /api/users/cart/remove/:itemId` - **Remove item from cart**

#### **Favorites Endpoints** (`/api/users/favorites/*`):
- `PUT /api/users/favorites` - **Update favorites list**
- `POST /api/users/favorites/add` - **Add product to favorites**
- `DELETE /api/users/favorites/remove/:productId` - **Remove from favorites**

#### **Portfolio Endpoints**:
- `/api/categories/*` - Category CRUD operations
- `/api/works/*` - Portfolio work management
- `/api/images/*` - Image upload and management
- `/api/texts/*` - Text content management
- `/api/public/*` - Public-facing endpoints

## User Management & E-commerce Features

### User Registration & Authentication
```typescript
// User registration with validation
{
  name: string,           // Full name (min 2 chars)
  email: string,          // Valid email format
  password: string,       // Min 6 chars
  confirmPassword: string // Must match password
}

// User login
{
  email: string,    // Email address
  password: string  // User password
}

// Response includes JWT token + user profile
{
  token: string,
  user: UserProfile
}
```

### Shopping Cart Management
```typescript
// Cart item structure
interface CartItem {
  id: string,           // Unique cart item ID
  productId: string,    // Product identifier
  productName: string,  // Product name
  quantity: number,     // Item quantity
  price: number,        // Item price
  imageUrl?: string     // Optional product image
}

// Cart operations
- Add items to cart with automatic quantity updates
- Remove specific items by cart item ID
- Update entire cart contents
- Persistent cart storage in user profile
```

### Favorite Products
```typescript
// Favorites are stored as array of product IDs
favoriteProducts: string[]

// Operations
- Add product to favorites (prevents duplicates)
- Remove product from favorites
- Update entire favorites list
- Persistent favorites storage in user profile
```

### Admin Dashboard - User Statistics
```typescript
// User statistics interface
interface UserStats {
  totalUsers: number,
  activeUsers: number,
  inactiveUsers: number,
  verifiedUsers: number,
  unverifiedUsers: number,
  usersRegisteredToday: number,
  usersRegisteredThisWeek: number,
  usersRegisteredThisMonth: number,
  recentRegistrations: UserProfile[]
}
```

### Database Considerations
- **SQLite for Development**: Fast setup, no external dependencies
- **MySQL for Production**: Scalable, production-ready
- **JSON Fields**: Shopping cart and favorites stored as JSON strings for SQLite compatibility
- **Type Safety**: Custom parsing with error handling for JSON fields
- **Indexes**: Proper indexing on frequently queried fields (email, isActive, createdAt)

### API Response Format
All endpoints follow consistent response structure:
```typescript
{
  message: string,              // Success/error message
  data?: any,                   // Response data
  error?: string,               // Error message
  meta?: PaginationMeta         // Pagination info
}
```

### Error Handling
- **ValidationError**: Input validation failures (400)
- **AuthenticationError**: Auth failures (401)
- **NotFoundError**: Resource not found (404)
- **ConflictError**: Duplicate resources (409)
- **DatabaseError**: DB operation failures (500)

### Security Measures
- Password hashing with bcrypt (12 rounds)
- JWT tokens with 7-day expiration
- Input validation at controller level
- SQL injection protection via Prisma
- No sensitive data exposure (password hashes hidden)
- Separate admin and user authentication contexts

## Usage Examples

### Admin Authentication & User Management
```bash
# Admin login
curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/admin/login \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"username": "admin", "password": "admin123"}'

# Get user statistics for dashboard
curl -X GET http://localhost:3000/api/admin/users/stats \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer ADMIN_JWT_TOKEN"

# Get all users with pagination
curl -X GET "http://localhost:3000/api/admin/users?page=1&limit=20" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer ADMIN_JWT_TOKEN"

# Deactivate user
curl -X PUT http://localhost:3000/api/admin/users/USER_ID/deactivate \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer ADMIN_JWT_TOKEN"
```

### User Registration & Authentication
```bash
# User registration
curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/users/register \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "name": "John Doe",
    "email": "john@example.com",
    "password": "password123",
    "confirmPassword": "password123"
  }'

# User login
curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/users/login \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"email": "john@example.com", "password": "password123"}'

# Get user profile
curl -X GET http://localhost:3000/api/users/profile \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer USER_JWT_TOKEN"
```

### Shopping Cart Operations
```bash
# Add item to cart
curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/users/cart/add \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer USER_JWT_TOKEN" \
  -d '{
    "productId": "product-1",
    "productName": "Sample Product",
    "quantity": 2,
    "price": 29.99,
    "imageUrl": "https://example.com/image.jpg"
  }'

# Remove item from cart
curl -X DELETE http://localhost:3000/api/users/cart/remove/CART_ITEM_ID \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer USER_JWT_TOKEN"
```

### Favorites Management
```bash
# Add to favorites
curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/users/favorites/add \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer USER_JWT_TOKEN" \
  -d '{"productId": "product-1"}'

# Remove from favorites
curl -X DELETE http://localhost:3000/api/users/favorites/remove/product-1 \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer USER_JWT_TOKEN"
```

